25. JOB ENVELOPE
Every job contains:
job_id
project_id
revision_id
model_version_id
job_type
priority
attempt
payload
created_at
started_at
completed_at
The model version is mandatory for any job operating on project geometry or documentation.

26. JOB IDEMPOTENCY
Jobs must be safely retryable.
A job execution must not create duplicate:
revisions
drawings
document packages
validation runs
events
when retried.
The job system therefore uses:
job_id
idempotency_key
source_revision
source_model_version
to identify execution state.

27. JOB FAILURE
Failed jobs transition to:
FAILED
with:
error_code
error_message
retryable
attempt_count
failure_context
Transient infrastructure failures may be retried.
Deterministic domain failures must not be blindly retried.

28. DEAD-LETTER PROCESSING
Jobs exceeding their retry policy enter:
DEAD_LETTER
The dead-letter record preserves:
original_job_id
project_id
revision_id
model_version_id
failure_history
payload_hash
This prevents silent disappearance of failed processing.

29. WORKER EXECUTION MODEL
Workers execute specialized jobs.
Conceptually:
Worker
 ↓
Load Job
 ↓
Verify Model Version
 ↓
Load Required State
 ↓
Execute Engine
 ↓
Validate Output
 ↓
Persist Derived State
 ↓
Emit Event
 ↓
Complete Job

30. STALE JOB PROTECTION
Before committing results, a worker verifies:
project_id
revision_id
model_version_id
remain valid.
If the project has advanced beyond the job's source model:
STALE
The worker must not silently promote the stale result to current state.

