38. DOCUMENTATION REGENERATION
When a model modification affects documentation:
MODEL CHANGE
 ↓
IMPACT ANALYSIS
 ↓
DIRTY VIEWS
 ↓
REGENERATE DRAWINGS
 ↓
REVALIDATE
 ↓
REBUILD PACKAGE
Unaffected documentation may remain unchanged where provenance permits.

39. REDLINE EXECUTION
A redline is treated as an instruction against project state.
The lifecycle is:
OPEN
 ↓
INTERPRETING
 ↓
PROPOSED
 ↓
IMPLEMENTING
 ↓
VALIDATING
 ↓
RESOLVED
A redline cannot be marked resolved merely because Aria generated a response.
The underlying project modification must be completed and validated.

40. REDLINE IMPACT
Every redline resolution records:
redline_id
command_id
source_revision
result_revision
implemented_changes
validation_results
This creates a traceable chain from human markup to model modification.

41. EVENT BUS
The runtime emits domain events after successful state transitions.
Initial events include:
PROJECT_CREATED
REQUIREMENT_CREATED
MODEL_CHANGED
REVISION_CREATED
COMMAND_COMPLETED
REDLINE_CREATED
REDLINE_RESOLVED
VALIDATION_STARTED
VALIDATION_COMPLETED
DRAWING_GENERATED
DOCUMENT_PACKAGE_GENERATED
ACCEPTANCE_RECORDED

42. EVENT PRINCIPLE
Events describe what happened.
Commands describe what should happen.
Therefore:
COMMAND
is an instruction.
EVENT
is an immutable historical fact within the application record.
The two must not be conflated.

43. EVENT PAYLOAD
An event contains:
event_id
event_type
project_id
revision_id
object_id
actor_id
timestamp
payload
schema_version
The payload must contain sufficient information for downstream consumers without exposing unnecessary private data.

44. AUDIT PIPELINE
Every material project mutation produces an audit event.
The chain becomes:
COMMAND
 ↓
DOMAIN MUTATION
 ↓
REVISION
 ↓
CHANGE RECORD
 ↓
AUDIT EVENT
This permits reconstruction of how the current state was produced.

