66. UNIT OF WORK
The transaction boundary shall be represented through a Unit of Work abstraction.
Conceptually:
with unit_of_work:
    project = projects.get(project_id)
    command_service.execute(command)
    unit_of_work.commit()
The Unit of Work owns transaction coordination.

67. DATABASE SESSION RULE
HTTP handlers must not directly manage arbitrary PostgreSQL transactions.
Application services receive the appropriate Unit of Work or transaction context.
This keeps persistence mechanics outside the API layer.

68. CACHE STRATEGY
Caching is permitted for:
read-heavy reference data
code metadata
sheet templates
static configuration
non-authoritative derived information
The cache must never become the authoritative source for project state.

69. PROJECT STATE AUTHORITY
The authoritative hierarchy remains:
POSTGRESQL PROJECT MODEL
        ↓
REVISION HISTORY
        ↓
DERIVED ARTIFACTS
Redis and caches are disposable execution infrastructure.

